.TH STATUS-VNC-SESSION.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
status\-vnc\-session.sh \- report control\-room VNC session state in a parseable form
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B status\-vnc\-session.sh
.I name display
.RI [ "name display" ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each pair prints one line
.PP
.EX
NAME|:DISPLAY|PORT|STATE|RESPONDER
.EE
.PP
with
.I PORT
= 5900 +
.IR display ,
.I STATE
.B running
or
.B stopped
from
.BR "vncserver \-list" ,
and
.I RESPONDER
.BR alive ,
.B dead
(pid file present, process gone) or
.B none
(no pid file).
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.crs/vnc\-responder\-:N.pid
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 when the argument count is zero or odd.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
status\-vnc\-session.sh dcs\-main 1 shift\-main 2 trig\-main 3
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-vnc\-session.sh (1),
.BR crs\-remote (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
